00:12:06,280 --> 00:12:10,200
Turns out Bartholomew Kuma was
on our side the whole time.

257
00:12:10,560 --> 00:12:11,840
A few days back.

258
00:12:12,140 --> 00:12:15,157
When I made it to the Sunny,
I couldn't believe my eyes.

259
00:12:15,240 --> 00:12:16,660
He was right there.

260
00:12:18,120 --> 00:12:19,840
I've been waiting for you.

261
00:12:21,420 --> 00:12:23,361
What the hell are you doing here?

262
00:12:25,080 --> 00:12:26,315
Mission accomplished.

263
00:12:31,020 --> 00:12:32,520
You saw for yourself.

264
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:35,609
There wasn't a single
scratch on the Sunny.

265
00:12:35,740 --> 00:12:38,093
Later, Rayleigh gave me the whole story.

266
00:12:38,520 --> 00:12:41,120
I am a member of the Revolutionary Army.

267
00:12:41,480 --> 00:12:45,177
If it's within my power, I want to
help the Straw Hats escape from here.

268
00:12:45,260 --> 00:12:49,157
You guys probably knew that something
was up, but now we know the truth.

269
00:12:49,240 --> 00:12:52,300
He saved the Sunny,
and he saved our lives.

270
00:12:52,500 --> 00:12:55,559
And then, after we were
sent flying from the island,

271
00:12:56,120 --> 00:12:59,473
Kuma paid Rayleigh a visit
and dropped another bombshell.

272
00:13:00,580 --> 00:13:01,857
I don't have much time.

273
00:13:01,940 --> 00:13:03,100
Not as myself.

274
00:13:03,560 --> 00:13:06,440
The details are a little
sketchy, but evidently,

275
00:13:06,620 --> 00:13:08,855
Kuma surrendered his body to the Navy.

276
00:13:09,120 --> 00:13:13,238
They used him as an experiment and
replaced his body parts one by one.

277
00:13:13,400 --> 00:13:15,617
By the time the War of
the Best rolled around,

278
00:13:15,700 --> 00:13:18,760
his personality had been
completely erased. Wait!

279
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:23,217
He knew where he sent us, but he didn't
know what we'd do once we got there,

280
00:13:23,300 --> 00:13:25,017
or that we would even make it back!

281
00:13:25,100 --> 00:13:29,317
And you said his personality was taken
away, but he still protected the Sunny?

282
00:13:29,400 --> 00:13:32,900
The guy who worked on him is
this dude named Dr. Vegapunk,

283
00:13:33,020 --> 00:13:35,257
and Kuma must have made
a deal with him because

284
00:13:35,340 --> 00:13:37,937
he programmed one final
mission into his brain.

285
00:13:38,020 --> 00:13:41,177
Defend the Thousand Sunny
from any attackers until

286
00:13:41,260 --> 00:13:44,084
the moment that a straw
hat returns to claim it.

287
00:13:44,300 --> 00:13:48,217
So even though he's been reduced
to a living weapon with no memory,

288
00:13:48,300 --> 00:13:50,535
he's been carrying out his own orders,

289
00:13:50,620 --> 00:13:54,940
protecting our ship for the past
two years to fulfill his last wish.

290
00:13:55,360 --> 00:13:56,200
But why?

291
00:13:56,440 --> 00:13:57,737
He barely knew us.

292
00:13:57,820 --> 00:14:00,780
I mean, why'd it matter
to him? I don't know.

293
00:14:01,220 --> 00:14:02,637
Maybe it's because of Luffy.

294
00:14:02,720 --> 00:14:05,037
You said Kuma was part of
the Revolutionary Army,

295
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:08,120
and Luffy's dad is the
leader of those guys, right?

296
00:14:08,660 --> 00:14:10,484
I don't know much about my dad,

297
00:14:10,640 --> 00:14:13,337
but it seems like that robot
bear dude was a good guy,

298
00:14:13,420 --> 00:14:15,891
so he can't be too bad if they're friends.

299
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:16,830
Kuma.

300
00:14:16,980 --> 00:14:18,480
The bottom line is,

301
00:14:18,740 --> 00:14:22,397
our survival and all the things we
accomplished in the past two years,

302
00:14:22,480 --> 00:14:23,310
we owe to him.

303
00:14:23,700 --> 00:14:26,465
Whatever his reason was,
we should be grateful.

304
00:14:26,680 --> 00:14:28,677
And we may never find out the truth,

305
00:14:28,760 --> 00:14:31,917
because it's not like we can ask
him to explain himself anymore.

306
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:35,317
All we can do now is
honor his memory and know

307
00:14:35,400 --> 00:14:37,988
that Bartholomew Kuma
was our greatest ally,

308
00:14:38,300 --> 00:14:40,712
until he took his last breath as a human.

309
00:14:41,520 --> 00:14:44,837
Unfortunately, we'll never be able to
thank him since he'll just be a weapon,

310
00:14:44,920 --> 00:14:47,449
and likely our enemy
the next time we meet.

311
00:14:48,360 --> 00:14:49,948
That's all I wanted to say.

312
00:14:50,040 --> 00:14:52,097
Kind of a lot to work through
all at once, isn't it?

313
00:14:52,180 --> 00:14:55,777
Someday, I hope we can at least
find out the rest of the story.

314
00:14:55,860 --> 00:14:58,500
Oh, you're awake. Good. Have some lunch.

315
00:14:58,660 --> 00:14:59,960
It's from Amazon Lily.

316
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:01,820
Oh, Amazon Lily.

317
00:15:02,020 --> 00:15:03,397
The island with all the women.

318
00:15:03,480 --> 00:15:04,997
Of course that's where he sent you.

319
00:15:05,080 --> 00:15:07,037
Do you know where I was
these past two years?

320
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:10,257
Because I'm kind of thinking Kuma's
not such a good friend after all.

321
00:15:10,340 --> 00:15:13,317
In fact, if he were here right now,
I'd like to kick his metal face in!

322
00:15:13,400 --> 00:15:16,017
Now, now, Sanji, we've all
had our share of troubles.

323
00:15:16,100 --> 00:15:19,097
Before I became a pop music
sensation, I was trapped in a cage.

324
00:15:19,180 --> 00:15:22,337
Still, the only thing that matters
now is the voyage awaiting us.

325
00:15:22,420 --> 00:15:23,250
Straight ahead!

326
00:15:23,333 --> 00:15:25,940
Brother, look! It's them! I know!

327
00:15:26,240 --> 00:15:28,257
Like you said, they're straight ahead.

328
00:15:28,340 --> 00:15:29,516
You think I'm blind?

329
00:15:30,700 --> 00:15:34,097
Looks like we'll be sailing
with the Straw Hats after all.

330
00:15:34,180 --> 00:15:36,480
Wow, how far down are we?

331
00:15:36,660 --> 00:15:39,760
I don't know, but it's
getting darker and darker.

332
00:15:40,600 --> 00:15:42,337
We passed the photic zone,

333
00:15:42,420 --> 00:15:45,677
and it looks like we're around
the bottom of the a-photic zone.

334
00:15:45,760 --> 00:15:47,995
About a thousand meters, give or take.

335
00:15:49,180 --> 00:15:52,437
Quiet and the sunny
itself feels oddly still.

336
00:15:52,520 --> 00:15:55,277
It's almost like floating in the sky.

337
00:15:55,360 --> 00:15:57,357
Hey look it's a whale.

338
00:15:57,440 --> 00:15:59,437
It's just like the moon.

339
00:15:59,520 --> 00:16:01,777
Nah it looks more like white beard.

340
00:16:01,860 --> 00:16:04,917
Wait a sec what is that thing?

341
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:05,830
A fish.

342
00:16:05,913 --> 00:16:10,197
No are you ready we only
get one shot at this?

343
00:16:10,280 --> 00:16:12,877
Ready brother ready captain.

344
00:16:12,960 --> 00:16:14,297
Before you say anything.

345
00:16:14,380 --> 00:16:15,917
I know what you're thinking.

346
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:18,235
Just shoot them and they'll all drown.

347
00:16:18,400 --> 00:16:22,165
They're wanted dead or alive after
all, so why not let them die?

348
00:16:22,540 --> 00:16:27,097
Well, that wouldn't do it all, because
the Navy wouldn't know who killed them.

349
00:16:27,180 --> 00:16:30,637
We have to deliver their heads
personally on a silver platter.

350
00:16:30,720 --> 00:16:32,240
Then they will fear us.

351
00:16:32,400 --> 00:16:35,320
The whole world will do our strength.

352
00:16:36,240 --> 00:16:38,977
We'll take them out before
they suspect a thing.

353
00:16:39,060 --> 00:16:43,620
My big smiling face is the last
thing they'll see before they die.

354
00:16:47,360 --> 00:16:52,520
Hey, you guys, there's a ship looking
thing coming our way what you sure?

355
00:16:52,780 --> 00:16:54,956
Why don't you come look for yourself?

356
00:17:01,720 --> 00:17:03,160
It's a pirate ship!

357
00:17:03,540 --> 00:17:05,257
They're ramming straight into us!

358
00:17:05,340 --> 00:17:06,620
Go away you morons!

359
00:17:06,800 --> 00:17:08,624
You're gonna make us all drown!

360
00:17:09,020 --> 00:17:12,817
They're not trying to break our
ship, they're trying to board it!

361
00:17:12,900 --> 00:17:14,180
Tumit? Who are they?

362
00:17:14,300 --> 00:17:16,500
Keep it up, Seacow! Yeah!

363
00:17:17,240 --> 00:17:18,517
You think they want to board the ship?

364
00:17:18,600 --> 00:17:19,430
Seacow?

365
00:17:20,480 --> 00:17:22,440
I know that noise from somewhere.

366
00:17:25,880 --> 00:17:26,710
Good.

367
00:17:27,140 --> 00:17:28,720
Is everybody ready?

368
00:17:29,340 --> 00:17:30,170
Yeah!

369
00:17:30,500 --> 00:17:31,600
Mama, it's me!

370
00:17:31,740 --> 00:17:32,717
We've met before!

371
00:17:32,800 --> 00:17:35,035
You're from the Arlong Pirates, right?

372
00:17:35,380 --> 00:17:36,210
Nami!

373
00:17:36,293 --> 00:17:37,940
I was at Arlong Park!

374
00:17:40,320 --> 00:17:43,438
Hey, Luffy, doesn't that
thing look kind of familiar?

375
00:17:43,880 --> 00:17:44,900
I don't know.

376
00:17:48,500 --> 00:17:50,080
Go, go, pistol!

377
00:17:53,720 --> 00:17:56,540
Let's pay our new friends
a visit, shall we?

378
00:17:58,800 --> 00:18:00,153
Let's stay out of here!

379
00:18:00,880 --> 00:18:02,580
There's no time to waste!

380
00:18:02,800 --> 00:18:04,020
Follow my lead!

381
00:18:06,500 --> 00:18:07,330
Fools!

382
00:18:07,460 --> 00:18:09,197
They're completely dumbfounded!

383
00:18:09,280 --> 00:18:13,497
If they're gonna sit there catching flies,
then we'll strike while the iron is hot!

384
00:18:13,580 --> 00:18:16,620
We'll smite this entire crew, right now!

385
00:18:20,560 --> 00:18:22,200
Come along, men!

386
00:18:22,420 --> 00:18:24,400
We'll make the beggars for mercy!

387
00:18:29,940 --> 00:18:32,317
What's wrong, Skull? Don't panic!

388
00:18:32,400 --> 00:18:33,780
That's not good.

389
00:18:34,080 --> 00:18:36,177
We have Captain Carable
on the ship back there.

390
00:18:36,260 --> 00:18:37,090
Never!

391
00:18:41,420 --> 00:18:43,920
Now, it's time for a little greeting.

392
00:18:44,560 --> 00:18:46,140
Fire the Gatling gun, men!

393
00:18:46,720 --> 00:18:48,360
Shower them in bullets!

394
00:18:49,380 --> 00:18:51,700
I want every last one of them dead!

395
00:18:52,280 --> 00:18:54,300
Send these Straw Hats to hell!

396
00:19:04,880 --> 00:19:05,710
No! Wait!

397
00:19:05,860 --> 00:19:07,937
You're not going to throw
me into the water, are you?

398
00:19:08,020 --> 00:19:09,497
Please don't do that to me, my friend!

399
00:19:09,580 --> 00:19:10,521
I'm begging you!

400
00:19:10,620 --> 00:19:12,796
By the way, you're very good-looking!

401
00:19:13,060 --> 00:19:17,119
I'm sure someone like you understands
the value of human life, right?

402
00:19:17,380 --> 00:19:18,210
Emphasize!

403
00:19:18,293 --> 00:19:19,520
The gods are watching!

404
00:19:19,740 --> 00:19:21,269
You'll be judged for this!

405
00:19:21,900 --> 00:19:24,194
Oh, make up your freaking mind already!

406
00:19:24,420 --> 00:19:28,117
Weren't you just about to fire your Gatling
gun and blast to saw the kingdom come?

407
00:19:28,200 --> 00:19:32,940
Anyway, tell me, I know you're the captain
of that ship, but what's your name?

408
00:19:33,360 --> 00:19:34,680
That's Roro no Zoro!

409
00:19:36,480 --> 00:19:37,617
Don't be ridiculous!

410
00:19:37,700 --> 00:19:40,437
What in the world makes you
think I would be the captain?

411
00:19:40,520 --> 00:19:41,660
I'm... Oh!

412
00:19:42,080 --> 00:19:43,757
Those ruffians were keeping me as a...

413
00:19:43,840 --> 00:19:46,940
a slave! That's it! Boy! Ooh!

414
00:19:47,160 --> 00:19:48,160
Glad that's over!

415
00:19:48,380 --> 00:19:49,580
Say, how's this?

416
00:19:49,800 --> 00:19:53,297
Do you think I could stay on this nice
ship with you all for a little while?

417
00:19:53,380 --> 00:19:55,280
Huh? Please? Wow.

418
00:19:55,640 --> 00:19:58,052
I feel kind of sorry for this poor loser.

419
00:19:58,200 --> 00:19:59,640
HE'S OBVIOUSLY LYING!

420
00:19:59,740 --> 00:20:00,677
ARE YOU CRAZY?!

421
00:20:00,760 --> 00:20:01,757
WHAT?!

422
00:20:01,840 --> 00:20:03,097
SERIOUSLY?!

423
00:20:03,180 --> 00:20:04,533
Hey, I have a question.

424
00:20:04,740 --> 00:20:07,577
Where'd that giant sea cow
pulling your ship come from?

425
00:20:07,660 --> 00:20:08,490
Hello?

426
00:20:10,740 --> 00:20:11,820
Oh, my.

427
00:20:12,900 --> 00:20:14,300
Who's this vixen?

428
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:17,620
I take it you're the famous cat burglar.

429
00:20:17,800 --> 00:20:18,680
Watch it, pal!

430
00:20:18,860 --> 00:20:22,737
Nobody's allowed to drool over our
beautiful navigator except for me!

431
00:20:22,820 --> 00:20:23,800
Don't worry.

432
00:20:24,320 --> 00:20:26,080
You're perfectly s -

433
00:20:27,860 --> 00:20:29,700
Hey, it's getting really old!

434
00:20:29,860 --> 00:20:30,740
Cut it out!

435
00:20:31,020 --> 00:20:32,860
The sea cow? Who knows?

436
00:20:33,020 --> 00:20:35,697
I just happened to catch it
out in the ocean somewhere.

437
00:20:35,780 --> 00:20:37,133
When you're underwater,

438
00:20:37,340 --> 00:20:41,397
having a sea monster pull your ship
is the mark of an experienced captain.

439
00:20:41,480 --> 00:20:42,310
Huh?

440
00:20:43,060 --> 00:20:43,890
Awesome!

441
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:47,880
Stop it, sea cow!

442
00:20:48,220 --> 00:20:50,200
What's the problem? Oh, brother!

443
00:20:50,680 --> 00:20:52,980
We're on our way to rescue you!

444
00:20:53,700 --> 00:20:55,860
I'm gonna find a sea monster, too!

445
00:20:57,040 --> 00:20:59,687
What crazy ideas are
you hatching now, Luffy?

446
00:21:00,560 --> 00:21:05,380
We should try to rehabilitate him with
something a little less sexy. Hey, Nami,

447
00:21:05,500 --> 00:21:09,337
the direction we're taking isn't exactly
the same way the Log Pose is pointing.

448
00:21:09,420 --> 00:21:10,740
Oh, no problem.

449
00:21:11,080 --> 00:21:14,937
The correct course is technically
southwest, so we're in the clear.

450
00:21:15,020 --> 00:21:19,057
Yeah, but if we went in a straight line,
we could get there a whole lot faster,

451
00:21:19,140 --> 00:21:19,970
couldn't we?

452
00:21:20,053 --> 00:21:22,797
Well, if you go straight, you risk
getting swept away in a sea current.

453
00:21:22,880 --> 00:21:27,097
And if that should happen, you might run
into an underwater mountain or a volcano,

454
00:21:27,180 --> 00:21:28,010
see?

455
00:21:28,093 --> 00:21:28,923
That's why.

456
00:21:29,460 --> 00:21:30,290
Yikes!

457
00:21:30,373 --> 00:21:31,700
I'm with you on this one.

458
00:21:31,920 --> 00:21:34,117
Yeah, but I thought all the
currents here were dangerous.

459
00:21:34,200 --> 00:21:36,100
It is the Grand Line, after all.

460
00:21:36,360 --> 00:21:39,197
So are you saying that some
of them are actually stable?

461
00:21:39,280 --> 00:21:40,460
Well, this one is.

462
00:21:40,920 --> 00:21:42,580
Now you stay put. Hey!

463
00:21:42,800 --> 00:21:45,097
It's gonna start getting
colder from here on out,

464
00:21:45,180 --> 00:21:47,177
so make sure you put
on a coat or something.

465
00:21:47,260 --> 00:21:48,297
You bring up a good point.

466
00:21:48,380 --> 00:21:51,057
I'm already starting to
feel goosebumps on my skin.

467
00:21:51,140 --> 00:21:53,217
Well, except for I...

468
00:21:53,300 --> 00:21:56,241
You don't have any skin
because you're a skeleton.

469
00:21:58,880 --> 00:22:01,645
Chopper, skull jokes are
the only thing I have.

470
00:22:01,980 --> 00:22:04,098
Please don't take that away from me.

471
00:22:04,380 --> 00:22:07,040
We're going somewhere
cold, not the deep sea.

472
00:22:07,540 --> 00:22:10,177
Don't you guys know the
water's cold in the deep sea?

473
00:22:10,260 --> 00:22:11,537
It's just like a bathtub.

474
00:22:11,620 --> 00:22:13,997
Hot water rises and cold
sinks to the bottom.

475
00:22:14,080 --> 00:22:14,910
Aha,

476
00:22:14,993 --> 00:22:16,997
because heat rises and
there's not much sunlight,

477
00:22:17,080 --> 00:22:19,197
so there's nothing to
heat the water down here.

478
00:22:19,280 --> 00:22:23,117
The temperature's not the only thing
that's different at the bottom.

479
00:22:23,200 --> 00:22:25,318
You're not still depressed, are you?

480
00:22:25,520 --> 00:22:29,320
Once we move down, we'll find
something called deep currents.

481
00:22:29,620 --> 00:22:31,297
You don't run into them terribly often,

482
00:22:31,380 --> 00:22:34,177
but they're much larger
than the regular currents.

483
00:22:34,260 --> 00:22:35,090
Also,

484
00:22:35,173 --> 00:22:36,957
they're quite unique in that
their flow is completely

485
00:22:37,040 --> 00:22:39,577
independent of what you
see closer to the surface.

486
00:22:39,660 --> 00:22:42,397
Currents under the currents and
you even have a diagram, huh?

487
00:22:42,480 --> 00:22:44,362
You sure do know a lot of stuff.

488
00:22:45,620 --> 00:22:47,237
That's because I'm so old.

489
00:22:47,320 --> 00:22:50,849
Not only that, but all currents
are connected to each other.

490
00:22:50,960 --> 00:22:54,037
That doesn't mean they have
to flow in the same direction.

491
00:22:54,120 --> 00:22:56,500
They flow east, west, up and down.

492
00:22:57,420 --> 00:23:00,080
It's like a big long
dragon all tangled up.

493
00:23:00,640 --> 00:23:04,017
The deep currents tend to travel
at a surprisingly slow pace.

494
00:23:04,100 --> 00:23:05,577
After they reach the deep sea,

495
00:23:05,660 --> 00:23:08,137
it takes approximately
2,000 years before they

496
00:23:08,220 --> 00:23:10,817
finally make their way up
to the surface of the water.

497
00:23:10,900 --> 00:23:13,312
That makes me feel young again, actually.

498
00:23:13,560 --> 00:23:14,520
2,000?

499
00:23:15,380 --> 00:23:17,100
Yes, 2,000.

500
00:23:17,720 --> 00:23:18,960
And because of that,

501
00:23:19,080 --> 00:23:23,551
there are countless tales about what
lurks within those deep, dark currents.

502
00:23:25,480 --> 00:23:26,480
Monsters. Curses.

503
00:23:26,800 --> 00:23:28,900
The Wrath of the Undead.

504
00:23:30,240 --> 00:23:32,880
You mean the deep sea is haunted? What?

505
00:23:33,020 --> 00:23:34,780
The sea is haunted? Help!

506
00:23:34,900 --> 00:23:36,194
That sounds fun to me!

507
00:23:36,420 --> 00:23:37,361
Calm down, guys.

508
00:23:37,900 --> 00:23:40,397
I don't know anything about
the Wrath of the Undead,

509
00:23:40,480 --> 00:23:42,377
or whatever you're freaking out about,

510
00:23:42,460 --> 00:23:45,197
but I do know that we'll encounter
a downward-flowing current soon.

511
00:23:45,280 --> 00:23:49,100
Once we do, we should be able to
ride it down into the deep sea.

512
00:23:49,600 --> 00:23:52,953
She said something about deep
sea currents, I don't know.

513
00:23:53,100 --> 00:23:56,335
You morons can at least
pretend like you understand me.

514
00:23:57,740 --> 00:23:59,100
Nami, I see it.

515
00:23:59,660 --> 00:24:00,490
Really?

516
00:24:00,940 --> 00:24:02,160
Check it out!

517
00:24:03,420 --> 00:24:04,250
Amazing.

518
00:24:04,560 --> 00:24:06,800
This one's called the downward plume.

519
00:24:11,060 --> 00:24:13,160
It's almost like a giant waterfall.

520
00:24:16,600 --> 00:24:17,680
Except underwater!

521
00:24:21,460 --> 00:24:23,360
It's going so fast!

522
00:24:23,600 --> 00:24:29,060
The sea is like falling into the sea,
which doesn't make sense, but I like it!

523
00:24:30,800 --> 00:24:33,220
Mother Nature, you're one crazy lady!

524
00:24:33,380 --> 00:24:34,980
What a spectacular sight!

525
00:24:35,240 --> 00:24:38,337
And from the looks of it, I'd
say the stream runs barely deep.

526
00:24:38,420 --> 00:24:42,773
I've heard stories about these currents,
but they did not do them justice.

527
00:24:42,900 --> 00:24:44,557
It's crazy dark down there!

528
00:24:44,640 --> 00:24:46,977
The floor so far, you can't even see it!

529
00:24:47,060 --> 00:24:47,890
We're dead!

530
00:24:48,420 --> 00:24:52,596
At this speed, we're gonna get
pile-driven straight down to the bottom!

531
00:24:53,760 --> 00:24:56,860
You sure it's safe if we
just go with the flow?

532
00:24:57,120 --> 00:24:59,377
If you're worried about
the ship, don't be.

533
00:24:59,460 --> 00:25:01,977
Sunny was built from
the treasure tree, Adam.

534
00:25:02,060 --> 00:25:03,648
It's as tough as they come.

535
00:25:04,360 --> 00:25:05,190
Okay!

536
00:25:06,800 --> 00:25:07,840
Let's go!

537
00:25:08,660 --> 00:25:09,490
Oh?

538
00:25:09,880 --> 00:25:11,520
Is that crap?

539
00:25:11,940 --> 00:25:13,937
So it really does live down here.

540
00:25:14,020 --> 00:25:15,300
It's no legend.

541
00:25:21,620 --> 00:25:23,780
Please listen to me, Straw Hats.

542
00:25:23,940 --> 00:25:25,640
We have to turn back.

543
00:25:26,040 --> 00:25:28,200
We're gonna die. Oh, yeah.

544
00:25:28,440 --> 00:25:29,417
I forgot you were here.

545
00:25:29,500 --> 00:25:30,794
There's a sea monster.

546
00:25:35,140 --> 00:25:36,860
It's the Kraken.

547
00:25:38,880 --> 00:25:41,777
A legendary giant octopus monster.

548
00:25:41,860 --> 00:25:44,580
He made fish food out of those ships.

549
00:25:45,240 --> 00:25:46,877
They left for the new world.

550
00:25:46,960 --> 00:25:48,457
And never made it.

551
00:25:48,540 --> 00:25:50,217
Turn around, please.

552
00:25:50,300 --> 00:25:51,577
I'm not ready to die.

553
00:25:51,660 --> 00:25:52,817
I beg you.

554
00:25:52,900 --> 00:25:55,197
Just wait around for a couple days.

555
00:25:55,280 --> 00:25:56,917
And it'll probably go away.

556
00:25:57,000 --> 00:25:58,400
Shut up for a sec.

557
00:25:59,500 --> 00:26:01,377
I just had a perfect idea.

558
00:26:01,460 --> 00:26:02,290
Guys.

559
00:26:02,373 --> 00:26:04,900
We just have to capture it.

560
00:26:05,780 --> 00:26:06,610
Huh?

561
00:26:07,480 --> 00:26:09,580
Have you lost your mind, Loopy?

562
00:26:09,980 --> 00:26:12,877
If we catch it, we can teach
it how to pull the ship.

563
00:26:12,960 --> 00:26:14,160
Like hell we can.

564
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:18,057
I tell you, look at it, but
it's so ridiculously huge.

565
00:26:18,140 --> 00:26:20,177
I don't know how in the world
you can miss a damn thing.

566
00:26:20,260 --> 00:26:21,848
Yeah, I gotta get it, babe.

567
00:26:22,700 --> 00:26:24,020
I can't die.

568
00:26:24,340 --> 00:26:26,516
It must have been here for centuries.

569
00:26:26,720 --> 00:26:29,437
The Kraken shows have been
missed from all over the world.

570
00:26:29,520 --> 00:26:32,755
It's one of the most terrible
monsters that ever lived.
